SUMMARY:Whiteville Teen Science Cafe: Burning for Quail
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our next Teen Science Cafe\, “Burning for Quail”\, on Thursday\, October 8 at 6PM. During this program\, we will begin to answer the question\, “What does wildlife management mean?” Using quail as an example\, this presentation\, led by Hackney Deans\, will dive into what managing for this species entails\, the strategies being used today\, and how the successful management of one species can benefit the environment as a whole. There will be an interactive activity following the presentation and food will be provided. We hope to see you there! \nFor questions about this event\, contact the museum at 910-788-5100 or whiteville@naturalsciences.org. \nABOUT THE SPEAKER \nThis program is led by Hackney Deans\, a NC State graduate and Wildlife Biologist with Quail Forever. Hackney helps private landowners with the implementation of wildlife management plans across the southeastern coastal plain of North Carolina.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/whiteville-teen-science-cafe-burning-for-quail/
LOCATION:Whiteville\, 415 South Madison Street\, Whiteville\, NC\, 28472\, United States
CATEGORIES:Science Cafes,Teens
GEO:34.3258479;-78.7027078
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Whiteville 415 South Madison Street Whiteville NC 28472 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=415 South Madison Street:geo:-78.7027078,34.3258479
END:VEVENT
